Oliver Seiler writes about human-caused evolutionary pressures on
animals. I've heard that there's a variant oppossum that runs instead
of freezing when frightened--it's a better reaction for dealing
with highways.

I don't know if this is happening, but I would think that all those
many years of trophy hunting is selecting for smaller, smarter
deer.

I don't think that environmentalism has been around long enough
to select for "cuteness", but it would be interesting if that
happens, since I think that cuteness=neoteny and might go with
increased intelligence.

